  "triplesComment": "The clang target triple each bundle target is parsed under, so the MANGLED NAME of a declaration is asked of the compiler rather than inferred. Mangling is ABI-specific and not derivable: MSVC's scheme was never published, and an ILP32 target spells size_t and long differently from an LP64 one, so armv7 and wasm32 do not share arm64's symbols. Two targets may legitimately share a triple - the two web targets differ by threading, not by ABI.",
